# SIP with swapped celestial axes: DEC--TAN on pixel axis 1, RA---TAN on
# axis 2, asymmetric A/B and a rotated, skewed CD (synthetic, from the
# round-2 verifier probe zz_sip_swapped_nosuffix). SIP is defined on PIXEL axes
# 1,2 (A on the column offset u, B on the row offset v) whatever world axis
# they carry, so swapping A and B for a latitude-first header is wrong;
# a mutant doing that is off by 2.48 arcsec here.
# CTYPEs have no -SIP suffix (wcslib applies SIP anyway).
NOTE SIP on swapped celestial axes (nosuffix)
GRID 1 1024 9 1 1024 9
HEADER
NAXIS   = 2
NAXIS1  = 1024
NAXIS2  = 1024
CTYPE1  = 'DEC--TAN'
CTYPE2  = 'RA---TAN'
CRVAL1  = 30.0
CRVAL2  = 150.0
CRPIX1  = 512.5
CRPIX2  = 400.5
CD1_1   = 0.0002
CD1_2   = 0.00005
CD2_1   = -0.00003
CD2_2   = -0.00025
A_ORDER = 2
B_ORDER = 2
A_2_0   = 2e-5
A_1_1   = 1e-5
A_0_2   = -4e-6
B_0_2   = 3e-5
B_1_1   = -1e-5
B_2_0   = 5e-6
